# Games against computer pilots when the station flies the plane (domains/recreation). Each
# computer pilot's plane has its own ArduPlane SITL, and the computer pilot flies it through
# the same radio channels as the TX15: the sticks, the arm switch and the mode switch. The
# console's driver (domains/groundstation/console/src/expect.rs) starts the game in the sim over the sensor feed link,
# and sees the other planes as the operator does, on the tactical map.

Section: Games with ArduPilot
  When the station flies your plane, the [[computer pilots]] fly theirs with [[ArduPilot]]
  too. Each one has a T1-S VTOL of its own, with an autopilot of its own. It flies the plane
  with a radio, as you do with the TX15: the sticks, the arm switch and the mode buttons. So
  each plane takes the same time to get into the air.

  Press G in the window of the sim for a [[pylon race]], or T for a game of [[tag]]. The
  planes of the computer pilots stand on the field near the pilot box. The station shows
  them on the [[tactical map]], with the other aircraft.

Vocabulary:
  State: the opponents are in hand | on the ground | launching | flying | down
    Shows: on the ground: the markers of the computer pilots' planes stand on the field near the pilot box, at 0 m
    Shows: flying: the markers of the computer pilots' planes climb above 5 m and fly away

Background:
  Given the console is connected to a VTOL on the ground
  And the TX15 is ready
